==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|urj-fin-pro|*kaikki}}, borrowed from {{der|fi|bat-pro|*kajakas|*kajakei}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{fi-pronunciation|a=LL-Q1412 (fin)-Susannaanas-kaikki.wav}}

===Pronoun===
{{fi-pron}}

# {{lb|fi|indefinite|uncountable}} [[everything]] {{q|in the singular}}
#: {{ux|fi|Tänään '''kaikki''' menee pieleen.|Today '''everything''' is going wrong.}}
#: {{ux|fi|Vihaan '''kaikkea'''.|I hate '''everything'''.}}
#: {{uxi|fi|eikä tässä vielä '''kaikki'''|but wait, there's more|lit=and this is not '''everything''' yet}}
# {{lb|fi|indefinite}} [[everyone]], [[everybody]] {{q|in the plural, except the nominative form is in the singular, but verbs in the plural form}}
#: {{ux|fi|'''Kaikki''' olivat täällä.|'''Everyone''' was here.}}
#: {{ux|fi|Vihaan '''kaikkia'''.|I hate '''everyone'''.}}
# {{lb|fi|in compounds}} [[all-]], [[omni-]]

===Determiner===
{{head|fi|determiner}}

# [[all]]
#: {{ux|fi|'''Kaikki''' sukkani löytyivät.|'''All''' my socks were found.}}
#: {{ux|fi|Yhtäkkiä '''kaikki''' vesi vyöryi huoneistoon.|Suddenly '''all''' the water ran into the apartment.}}

====Usage notes====
* The pronoun also has the nominative plural form {{m|fi||kaiket}}, which is used only in some phrases, e.g. {{m|fi|kaiket [[päivä]]t||every day, all the time, day after day, for days on end}}.

====Declension====
{{fi-decl-ovi|kai|kk|k|a|pos=adj}}
Also forms: {{m|fi|kaikkialla}} (superessive singular), {{m|fi|kaikkialle}} (sublative singular), {{m|fi|kaikkialta}} (delative singular), {{m|fi|kaiketi}} (caritive).

====Synonyms====
* {{s|everyone}} {{l|fi|jokainen}}

====Antonyms====
* {{as|all, everything}} {{l|fi|mikään}}
* {{as|everyone}} {{l|fi|kukaan}}

